   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying your name",
     "texto": [
      "**Benim adım Anna** means «my name is Anna»; in conversation **Adım Anna** is usually enough.",
      "**Ben Anna'yım** («I am Anna») adds a personal ending to the name. After a proper name, the suffix is separated with an apostrophe: **Anna'yım**.",
      "**Memnun oldum** means «pleased to meet you»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking someone's name",
     "texto": [
      "**Adın ne?** = what's your name? (informal). **Adınız ne?** is the polite or plural form.",
      "**Ne?** means «what?». In Turkish, many yes/no questions use the separate particle **mi/mı/mu/mü**; in this lesson it appears in **Türk müsün?** («Are you Turkish?»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
